    "reply": "The analysis is saved. Now let me provide the useful prose answer with the optional decision-paths structure.\n## Screening before release \u2014 which release path is available\n**The rule.** Section 4 of the fictional supplier contract requires the operator (Harbor) to **complete screening before releasing a payment**. Section 5 backs this up by requiring a dated screening record, which lets the sequencing be audited. So the baseline is a sequencing obligation: screening first, release second.\n**The exception.** The contract allows a **limited pilot** of at most **ten test accounts** to use **manual screening**. Two constraints matter: the cap at ten accounts, and the fact that the exception **does not waive screening** \u2014 the pilot still screens, just manually. It is not a screening-free release.\n**The unknown timing.** The pivot is whether screening completes before release. That is recorded as an open supporting question and an open fact \u2014 Product has not confirmed it. Until answered, the full-release path cannot be confirmed as available.\n**Two conditional routes.**\n- **Route 1 \u2014 Delayed release.** If screening does complete before release, Harbor may release through the normal path, satisfying Section 4. Cost: release waits on screening, so launch timing slips.\n- **Route 2 \u2014 Limited pilot.** If screening cannot be confirmed to complete before a full release, Harbor may still proceed with a pilot of at most ten test accounts using manual screening. This preserves learning and limits exposure, but it is capped and still requires screening.\n**Business alternative.** Treat the pilot as the first release and defer the wider rollout until screening timing is confirmed and the pilot's operational work (the separate pilot issue) is done. This keeps Harbor inside the contract while gathering data, at the cost of a smaller initial footprint.\n**Why the fact matters.** The order of screening and release decides which route is open. Screening-first opens the full release; otherwise only the capped manual-screening pilot is available. That is why confirming the timing is the single most useful next step.\n```decision-paths\n{\"issue_analysis\":{\"issue_id\":\"ISS-TIMING\",\"display_title\":\"Screening before release\",\"explanation\":\"Section 4 requires screening to complete before release; the only exception is a capped manual-screening pilot that does not waive screening. Whether screening completes first decides which release path is available.\",\"business_effect\":\"If screening completes first, Harbor can release through the normal path. If not, only a pilot of at most ten test accounts using manual screening is available, deferring the wider rollout.\",\"tests\":[{\"test_id\":\"test-seq\",\"title\":\"Screening-before-release sequencing\",\"summary\":\"The operator must complete screening before releasing a payment; the limited pilot (\u226410 test accounts, manual screening) is the only exception and does not waive screening.\",\"kind\":\"contract\",\"actor\":\"Harbor (operator)\",\"jurisdiction\":\"Fictional supplier contract\",\"effective_at\":\"Current contract term\",\"exceptions\":\"Limited pilot of at most ten test accounts may use manual screening; screening is not waived.\",\"applicability\":\"Harbor is the operator releasing payments under the fictional supplier contract, so Section 4's sequencing obligation and its pilot exception govern the available release path.\",\"claim_ids\":[],\"condition_ids\":[\"condition-screening\"]}],\"conditions\":[{\"condition_id\":\"condition-screening\",\"question\":\"Does screening complete before release?\",\"assessment\":\"unknown\",\"assessment_basis\":\"Recorded as an open supporting question and an open fact; Product has not confirmed whether screening completes before release.\",\"fact_ids\":[\"the internal record\",\"the internal record\"],\"question_ids\":[\"Q-SCREENING\"],\"claim_ids\":[]}],\"options\":[{\"option_id\":\"option-delayed\",\"title\":\"Delayed release (screening completes first)\",\"kind\":\"conditional_path\",\"condition_summary\":\"Screening completes before release\",\"requirements\":[{\"condition_id\":\"condition-screening\",\"state\":\"met\"}],\"combination\":\"all\",\"consequence\":\"Harbor may release payments through the normal path, satisfying Section 4's sequencing requirement.\",\"trade_off\":\"Release is delayed until screening finishes, so launch timing slips.\",\"remaining_work\":[\"Confirm screening completes before release\"],\"recommendation\":\"candidate\",\"recommendation_reason\":\"This is the contract-compliant full-release path, available only if the timing condition is met.\",\"claim_ids\":[],\"work_item_ids\":[]},{\"option_id\":\"option-pilot\",\"title\":\"Limited pilot (manual screening, \u226410 test accounts)\",\"kind\":\"conditional_path\",\"condition_summary\":\"Screening is not confirmed to complete before a full release\",\"requirements\":[{\"condition_id\":\"condition-screening\",\"state\":\"not_met\"}],\"combination\":\"all\",\"consequence\":\"Harbor may proceed with a pilot of at most ten test accounts using manual screening; screening is still required and the wider rollout is deferred.\",\"trade_off\":\"Capped at ten accounts and still requires screening; does not authorize a wider rollout.\",\"remaining_work\":[\"Complete pilot operational work (ISS-PILOT)\",\"Confirm screening timing before wider rollout\"],\"recommendation\":\"candidate\",\"recommendation_reason\":\"This is the only available path when screening timing is unconfirmed, preserving learning while limiting first-release exposure.\",\"claim_ids\":[],\"work_item_ids\":[]},{\"option_id\":\"option-pilot-first\",\"title\":\"Pilot as first release, defer wider rollout\",\"kind\":\"business_alternative\",\"condition_summary\":\"Business choice to use the pilot as the initial release regardless of timing\",\"requirements\":[],\"combination\":\"all\",\"consequence\":\"Harbor launches via the capped manual-screening pilot and defers the wider rollout until screening timing is confirmed and pilot operational work is complete.\",\"trade_off\":\"Smaller initial footprint and slower scale-up, but stays within the contract while gathering data.\",\"remaining_work\":[\"Confirm screening timing\",\"Complete pilot operational work (ISS-PILOT)\"],\"recommendation\":\"candidate\",\"recommendation_reason\":\"A business alternative that keeps Harbor compliant while preserving learning and limiting first-release risk.\",\"claim_ids\":[],\"work_item_ids\":[]}]}}\n```\nThe analysis is saved as a recommendation in the matter. The single most useful next step is confirming whether screening completes before release \u2014 that answer selects between the delayed-release and pilot routes.",
